  "chr7ins": "Genotype of the ~3.8 kb transposon insertion directly upstream of gsdf (the chr7-ins Y allele of Munby et al. 2021) from short reads. Read pairs crossing either junction, at both GT3a copies of the gsdf unit (NC_135173.1:50,765,050 and :50,786,787), are summed (0/0 absent, 0/1 heterozygous, 1/1 homozygous). In a fish with three or four gsdf copies the insertion allele is a smaller share of the reads than the model's one half, so a low-fraction heterozygote there can be called 0/0."
